WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
- What's the worst gift you ever got?

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.230
- Worst gift.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.230
- Well, one year my older
son tricked my younger son

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.923
and wrapped up a bunch
of avocados, bananas.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.953
So he essentially got
fruit salad for Christmas.

00:00:17.953 --> 00:00:19.020
(others laughing)

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.420
Yeah. That was, it was funny.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.340
- [Melissa] Well, it was
healthy. It was a healthy gift.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.360
- [Nia] A healthy gift!

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.370
- There you go, optimism.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.933
- Silver Lining Melissa.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.450
- No, I got a great gift from my sister.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.680
I won't say it's the worst gift.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.110
It was kind of like double, double whammy.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.234
Okay, she gave me a pair of shoes,

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:39.813
but then I opened the
box and they were worn.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.748
I was like, well, wait,

00:00:42.748 --> 00:00:44.940
did, did you wear these?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.320
She was like, "Well, you
said you liked them."

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.625
I was like, I.. but.. did they not?

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.790
They were worn, but I loved them.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.500
So I still wore 'em. I still kept it.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.377
- [Morris] There's silver
lining, silver lining.

00:00:54.377 --> 00:00:55.210
- [Nia] Did she go to the club

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.730
the night before gave you the shoes?

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.770
- I think she had worn them to school.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.720
She had worn them all over the place.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:01.553
- [Nia] Oh, wow.

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:02.580
- And I told her I liked them,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.073
but I didn't know that I
would get the same pair.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.680
- That's not right.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.000
Regina, what about you?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.500
- [Nia] That's not right, she said

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.820
- You know, I didn't get, you know what?

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.980
My brothers used to take my gifts

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.450
and give them to their girlfriend.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.534
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.670
- Yeah. I had a brother that would take,

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.147
the girlfriend would
come over and be like,

00:01:19.147 --> 00:01:20.460
"Look what your brother got me."

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.720
And I was like--

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.950
- [Nia] That's horrible.
- Isn't it?

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.453
It's horrible.

00:01:24.453 --> 00:01:25.470
- [Nia] That's terrible.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.956
- Yeah. But that's what happens. Look.

00:01:27.956 --> 00:01:29.373
Kelly is like.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.937
- That's how Regina looked
when it used to happen.

00:01:31.937 --> 00:01:32.820
She was confused.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:33.653
- [Regina] That was, that's right.

00:01:33.653 --> 00:01:36.180
- This is really bringing Kelly down.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.500
Don't come to our houses.
- Did you ever

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.482
call your brothers out?

00:01:38.482 --> 00:01:39.990
Did you ever call them out?

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.010
Like in front of them?

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:41.910
- Of course.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.320
Oh, not in front of the girl.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.450
No, I never could do it
in front of the girl.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.320
I would just go to 'em like.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.616
- She's so loyal.

00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:49.080
- I know.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.460
I couldn't do it in front of the girl,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.379
but I told my mother and my father.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.540
(audience laughing)

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.833
- And they did nothing.

00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:57.684
- They did nothing.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:01.200
- They would say "stop
taking your sister's."

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.870
I mean, they just got verbal reprimands.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:05.100
- What about you, Taye?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.453
What about your worst gift?

00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:11.010
- A pack of gum,
Bubblicious gum, one time.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.150
That was my worst gift.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.451
- Wow. What, you didn't like Bubblicious?

00:02:14.451 --> 00:02:15.780
- I wanted--

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.650
- I like Bubblicious.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.483
- [Nia And Melissa] I do too.

00:02:17.483 --> 00:02:18.510
- Bad-ass bubbles!

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:19.710
- I love Bubblicious.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.056
- Not for Christmas!

00:02:21.056 --> 00:02:22.720
(audience laughing)

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:23.553
- No, that's like,

00:02:23.553 --> 00:02:26.280
that should have been
like a stocking stuffer.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.310
- Something along those lines, yeah.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.570
- I never had a stocking.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.640
- I never had, we
couldn't afford all that.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.506
- We got the gift.

00:02:33.506 --> 00:02:34.750
- Never had a?

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.850
- I never had stocking.
- [Nia] No stocking.

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:36.870
Very few ornaments.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:38.872
- Kelly welcome to the hood, okay?

00:02:38.872 --> 00:02:39.807
(all laughing)

00:02:39.807 --> 00:02:41.040
- No, I grew up--

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.390
Hey, y'all are talking to someone

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.890
who grew up with no money.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.723
- Sorry Kelly.

00:02:44.723 --> 00:02:47.520
- I didn't grow up with any
money, but it's called credit.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.589
My parents would put stuff on credit.

00:02:50.589 --> 00:02:51.618
- We didn't get credit.

00:02:51.618 --> 00:02:53.310
We didn't, we didn't even have that.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.620
- One time my father
gave my mother a photo

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.530
of what she was gonna
what he was gonna get her.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.403
- Oh my God.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.370
- She liked it, she liked it.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.240
It was a nice desk.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.863
It didn't ever arrive, but.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.923
- My mother was really good at layaway.

00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:11.075
- Oh god, me too!

00:03:11.075 --> 00:03:12.150
- Yes, layaway.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.795
She be like, "We gon' put it on layaway."

00:03:13.795 --> 00:03:16.410
- There's no more layaway.
They should bring layaway back.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.460
- But your mother was good,

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.200
did she pick it up off of the layaway?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.040
- Most of the time.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.567
It took a while, it took a while.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.800
- But you got it.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.675
- That last payment was awesome.

00:03:24.675 --> 00:03:25.508
(all laughing)

